    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Setting up and repairing tufting machines: style set-up, needle bar and gauge parts, reblading and rehooking, setting loopers, knives and backing feed, and the pattern attachments. A person who has it changes a machine over to a new style and finds why it is streaking or skipping.', 'On the job as a tufting fixer or mechanic, after time as an operator; machine makers train mechanics.', ARRAY['Needle bars and gauge parts', 'Hook, looper and knife modules', 'Setting gauges', 'Pattern controllers']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Wiring 120- and 240-volt AC circuits: the panelboard, branch circuits to receptacles, lights and appliances, ground-fault and arc-fault protection, and the shore power or utility inlet. A person who has it wires to the electrical code, keeps polarity and grounding right and proves each circuit before it is energized.',
  how_learned = 'Electrical apprenticeships and programs; on the job at RV, boat and modular building plants, which wire to the RV and marine articles of the National Electrical Code and the ABYC standards.', tools = ARRAY['Panelboards and breakers', 'Nonmetallic cable and boxes', 'Receptacle and GFCI testers', 'Multimeters']
  WHERE name = 'Branch Circuit Wiring'
    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Wiring 120- and 240-volt AC circuits: the panelboard, branch circuits to receptacles, lights and appliances, ground-fault and arc-fault protection, and the shore power or utility inlet. A person who has it wires to the electrical code, keeps polarity and grounding right and proves each circuit before it is energized.', 'Electrical apprenticeships and programs; on the job at RV, boat and modular building plants, which wire to the RV and marine articles of the National Electrical Code and the ABYC standards.', ARRAY['Panelboards and breakers', 'Nonmetallic cable and boxes', 'Receptacle and GFCI testers', 'Multimeters']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Calculating how a site''s power system behaves from its one-line diagram: load flow, short-circuit currents, the coordination of protective devices and arc-flash energy. A person who has it can model the system, set the relays and breakers from the result and label the equipment.',
  how_learned = 'A power engineering course and the software vendor''s training, then on the job under a licensed engineer.', tools = ARRAY['Power system analysis software', 'One-line diagrams', 'Relay and breaker time-current curves', 'Equipment ratings and utility fault data']
  WHERE name = 'Power System Studies'
    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Calculating how a site''s power system behaves from its one-line diagram: load flow, short-circuit currents, the coordination of protective devices and arc-flash energy. A person who has it can model the system, set the relays and breakers from the result and label the equipment.', 'A power engineering course and the software vendor''s training, then on the job under a licensed engineer.', ARRAY['Power system analysis software', 'One-line diagrams', 'Relay and breaker time-current curves', 'Equipment ratings and utility fault data']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Running and servicing an industrial ammonia refrigeration plant: starting, loading and stopping screw and reciprocating compressors from their panels; watching suction and discharge pressures, condensers, vessels and defrost; draining oil and purging air; isolating and pumping down equipment for work; and keeping the logs and procedures the process safety rules require. A person who has it holds the rooms and the process at temperature and responds correctly to an ammonia leak.',
  how_learned = 'On the job under a senior operator; the Refrigerating Engineers and Technicians Association''s CARO, CIRO and CRST certifications; IIAR training. A plant with more than 10,000 pounds of ammonia falls under OSHA''s process safety management standard.', tools = ARRAY['Screw and reciprocating compressors', 'Evaporative condensers', 'Receivers, recirculators and evaporators', 'Compressor control panels', 'Ammonia detectors', 'Escape and air-purifying respirators']
  WHERE name = 'Ammonia Refrigeration System Operation'
    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Running and servicing an industrial ammonia refrigeration plant: starting, loading and stopping screw and reciprocating compressors from their panels; watching suction and discharge pressures, condensers, vessels and defrost; draining oil and purging air; isolating and pumping down equipment for work; and keeping the logs and procedures the process safety rules require. A person who has it holds the rooms and the process at temperature and responds correctly to an ammonia leak.', 'On the job under a senior operator; the Refrigerating Engineers and Technicians Association''s CARO, CIRO and CRST certifications; IIAR training. A plant with more than 10,000 pounds of ammonia falls under OSHA''s process safety management standard.', ARRAY['Screw and reciprocating compressors', 'Evaporative condensers', 'Receivers, recirculators and evaporators', 'Compressor control panels', 'Ammonia detectors', 'Escape and air-purifying respirators']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Running a building''s heating, cooling, ventilation and utility plant from its automation system: reading the graphics, trends and alarms, changing setpoints and schedules, and finding whether a complaint is the sensor, the controller or the equipment. A person who has it answers an alarm from the workstation first, trends a point before changing it, and leaves an override with a note and an end date.',
  how_learned = 'On the job on the site''s system; the control makers and their dealers teach operator and technician courses.', tools = ARRAY['Building automation workstations and graphics', 'Direct digital controllers', 'Temperature, pressure and flow sensors', 'Valve and damper actuators', 'Trend logs and alarm summaries']
  WHERE name = 'Building Automation System Operation'
    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Running a building''s heating, cooling, ventilation and utility plant from its automation system: reading the graphics, trends and alarms, changing setpoints and schedules, and finding whether a complaint is the sensor, the controller or the equipment. A person who has it answers an alarm from the workstation first, trends a point before changing it, and leaves an override with a note and an end date.', 'On the job on the site''s system; the control makers and their dealers teach operator and technician courses.', ARRAY['Building automation workstations and graphics', 'Direct digital controllers', 'Temperature, pressure and flow sensors', 'Valve and damper actuators', 'Trend logs and alarm summaries']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Testing a freight car''s air brake system with a single car test device to the code of the Association of American Railroads: charging, leakage, application and release, service and emergency, retainer and piston travel, then recording the test on the car. A person who has it finds a failed valve or a leak and replaces the part before the retest.',
  how_learned = 'On the job at a railcar shop, with the employer''s qualification to the AAR''s single car test; the federal freight brake rules (49 CFR Part 232) govern the work.', tools = ARRAY['Single car test devices', 'Air gauges and flow meters', 'Control valves and brake cylinders', 'Piston travel gauges']
  WHERE name = 'Railcar Air Brake Testing'
    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Testing a freight car''s air brake system with a single car test device to the code of the Association of American Railroads: charging, leakage, application and release, service and emergency, retainer and piston travel, then recording the test on the car. A person who has it finds a failed valve or a leak and replaces the part before the retest.', 'On the job at a railcar shop, with the employer''s qualification to the AAR''s single car test; the federal freight brake rules (49 CFR Part 232) govern the work.', ARRAY['Single car test devices', 'Air gauges and flow meters', 'Control valves and brake cylinders', 'Piston travel gauges']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Building and repairing the trucks a railcar rides on: setting side frames, bolster, springs and friction wedges, mounting wheelsets with their roller bearing adapters, and gauging wear against the limits of the AAR''s interchange rules. A person who has it jacks and blocks a car safely to change a wheelset.',
  how_learned = 'On the job at a railcar builder or repair shop.', tools = ARRAY['Car jacks and truck stands', 'Wheel and bearing gauges', 'Overhead cranes and lifting fixtures', 'Spring and wedge gauges']
  WHERE name = 'Railcar Truck Assembly'
    AND (description, how_learned, tools) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Building and repairing the trucks a railcar rides on: setting side frames, bolster, springs and friction wedges, mounting wheelsets with their roller bearing adapters, and gauging wear against the limits of the AAR''s interchange rules. A person who has it jacks and blocks a car safely to change a wheelset.', 'On the job at a railcar builder or repair shop.', ARRAY['Car jacks and truck stands', 'Wheel and bearing gauges', 'Overhead cranes and lifting fixtures', 'Spring and wedge gauges']);
UPDATE skills SET description = 'Removing, inspecting and fitting couplers, knuckles, yokes and draft gear: gauging contour and knuckle wear, applying the right pins, keys and retainers, and setting coupler height. A person who has it knows the condemning limits the interchange rules give.',
  how_learned = 'On the job at a railcar builder or repair shop.', tools = ARRAY['Coupler contour and knuckle gauges', 'Draft gear jacks and lifting tools', 'Coupler height gauges', 'Pins, keys and retainers']
  WHERE name = 'Coupler and Draft Gear Service'
